  "id": "COMPOUND:21375 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "Orotinin is shown to have a target relationship with HaCaT cells, which are a type of human skin cell line. The evidence suggests that Orotinin interacts with HaCaT cells, which in turn are targeted by multiple compounds, including those that have a target relationship with the CD276 antigen. These compounds are diverse, ranging from a complex flavonoid to a structured oxan-2-yl derivative, all of which ultimately lead to the CD276 antigen. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the CD276 antigen indicates a potential mechanism where Orotinin may influence cellular processes through these intermediates. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility that Orotinin exerts its effects via a complex network of molecular interactions, possibly modulating cellular signaling pathways that involve the CD276 antigen. The evidence supports a role for Orotinin in targeting HaCaT cells, which may be linked to the CD276 antigen through a series of molecular interactions that are not fully elucidated.",
